WEBVTT

00:16.460 --> 00:19.360
Taiyou ni me ga kurameba

00:19.360 --> 00:24.040
hikari no hate o shiru darou

00:24.040 --> 00:25.940
Hoshikuzu no nou

00:25.940 --> 00:31.780
Nante semai uchuu de boku wa ikiteru

00:31.780 --> 00:39.320
Dare ka zero kara hajimeru
koodo o sazukete kurenai ka

00:39.320 --> 00:41.890
Zoushoku sare sakuran

00:41.890 --> 00:45.920
Hako no naka shiseru koronii

00:45.920 --> 00:50.400
Kakan naki yume o ute

00:50.400 --> 00:53.570
Kodoku yo jibaku seyo

00:53.570 --> 00:57.970
Yubisaki no mirai ni

00:57.970 --> 01:01.810
donna sakurifaisu ga arou to

01:01.810 --> 01:05.480
Mune no oku de

01:05.480 --> 01:08.780
Kokoro koushin seyo

01:08.780 --> 01:12.920
Ippo kako no hibi ga

01:12.920 --> 01:15.920
toozakatte yukedomo

01:15.920 --> 01:22.990
Koishikarubeki kimi

01:49.190 --> 01:51.720
There are two kinds of humans.

01:51.720 --> 01:53.490
Humans who look good with fake ears on...

01:53.490 --> 01:55.860
and humans who don't.

01:55.860 --> 01:57.300
Don't mock me, bear-o!

01:57.300 --> 01:59.000
And there aren't any
two kinds like that, bear-o!

01:59.000 --> 02:00.670
I don't care one way or the other...

02:00.670 --> 02:04.030
I just want to know why I
have to wear these stupid things, too!

02:05.000 --> 02:07.470
Because this is a beastman town...

02:07.470 --> 02:11.680
and because a good disguise goes
a long way toward ensuring our safety.

02:11.680 --> 02:14.650
But those fake ears look
pretty good on you, Morte!

02:14.650 --> 02:18.150
There's no question in my mind you're the
kind of human who looks good with fake ears on.

02:18.150 --> 02:21.240
Didn't I just tell you there are
no two kinds like that, bear-o?!

02:25.760 --> 02:30.560
Are you sure the spring continent
is the right choice of destination?

02:30.560 --> 02:35.430
I realize that the spring continent
is the closest one to Bonak, but...

02:35.430 --> 02:38.540
Normally someone would
steer clear of the spring continent

02:38.540 --> 02:41.940
and head for the summer
or fall continents instead.

02:41.940 --> 02:45.080
But those three are no idiots.

02:45.080 --> 02:48.380
I think they'll take the opposite of the
opposite of what we'd normally expect...

02:48.380 --> 02:51.180
then do the opposite of that
and head for the spring continent.

02:51.180 --> 02:53.720
Don't you think you're
overthinking this a little?

02:53.720 --> 02:58.860
I really don't think they're as
smart as you seem to think they are.

02:58.860 --> 03:01.790
Well, even if they don't have the
brainpower to concoct a plan like that...

03:01.790 --> 03:07.060
there's still the will of the Destruct Code.

03:08.570 --> 03:13.530
"There are Two Kinds of Humans"

03:17.810 --> 03:19.110
Well, then?

03:19.110 --> 03:22.250
Where are we headed anyway, bear-o?

03:22.250 --> 03:25.720
What exactly is the final
destination of our journey, bear-o?

03:25.720 --> 03:30.090
I already told you...
all I know is the Destruct Code.

03:30.090 --> 03:33.730
It's what guides us along
the path to world destruction.

03:33.730 --> 03:36.730
So what you're saying is that the
messes the three of us have been through...

03:36.730 --> 03:40.390
are all because of the
guidance of that thing, bear-o?

03:42.130 --> 03:46.570
Well hey, at least coming to the spring
continent was the right call, don't you think?

03:46.570 --> 03:51.740
I mean, if you're gonna travel, you can't do
better than a warm and tranquil place like this!

03:51.740 --> 03:54.080
Why are you acting so carefree?

03:54.080 --> 03:56.080
Have you forgotten we're fugitives?

03:56.080 --> 03:59.070
We're fugitives completely
because of you, bear-o!

04:00.590 --> 04:03.120
Anyway, I was always told the spring continent

04:03.120 --> 04:06.250
was a place where the
cherry trees were spectacular...

04:06.860 --> 04:10.630
but I haven't seen a single cherry tree yet.

04:10.630 --> 04:15.430
And here I was thinking we could
go have a picnic under the cherry trees...

04:15.430 --> 04:18.440
Are you folks traveling beastmen?

04:18.440 --> 04:20.630
Y-Yes we are!

04:24.640 --> 04:28.880
All the cherry trees in this
town have been cut down.

04:28.880 --> 04:29.780
Huh?

04:29.780 --> 04:33.650
Cherry trees suck the lifeblood of
beastmen and use it to make their flowers...

04:33.650 --> 04:37.620
It's an old legend that
still lives on in this town.

04:37.620 --> 04:40.730
That's a common superstition, bear-o.
Back in my hometown...

04:40.730 --> 04:44.330
we had a saying that the ground
beneath a cherry tree in full bloom

04:44.330 --> 04:46.360
was filled with the
corpses of beastmen, bear-o.

04:46.360 --> 04:49.370
That's right... it's just something people say.

04:49.370 --> 04:54.470
And of course no one really took
that kind of thing very seriously before.

04:54.470 --> 04:58.140
But then the Frog Master
became the new lord of the town...

04:58.140 --> 05:00.650
and started telling everyone
the cherry trees were unlucky.

05:00.650 --> 05:04.980
So he cut down all the trees in town.

05:09.550 --> 05:12.060
My lord!

05:12.060 --> 05:13.490
We've just received word...

05:13.490 --> 05:17.160
that the World Salvation Committee
will be arriving in port at Vito tonight.

05:17.160 --> 05:20.230
And they will be heading for this
town sometime early tomorrow morning.

05:20.230 --> 05:23.500
The World Salvation Committee...

05:26.670 --> 05:32.840
Mmm... I really don't want them
stirring up trouble inside my territory.

05:36.450 --> 05:39.880
Man, I was really hoping we could
have a picnic under the cherry trees.

05:39.880 --> 05:43.880
I keep telling you... we didn't
come here to look at flowers!

05:52.800 --> 05:53.930
What?

05:53.930 --> 05:55.430
What's going on?

05:55.430 --> 05:56.590
Look at this!

05:57.640 --> 05:59.200
It's a cherry blossom!

05:59.200 --> 06:00.970
Over this way, bear-o!

06:13.750 --> 06:17.920
So why is this cherry tree still here
when all the others got cut down, bear-o?

06:17.920 --> 06:23.090
Who knows, but at least now we
can have our cherry blossom picnic!

06:23.090 --> 06:25.830
C'mon, Morte... stop making that face.

06:25.830 --> 06:28.430
Let's have some fun for a change!

06:28.430 --> 06:30.600
I mean, the whole reason
we're here on the spring continent...

06:30.600 --> 06:33.640
is because the Destruct Code led us here.

06:33.640 --> 06:37.740
You never know... maybe the Destruct
Code wanted to look at cherry blossoms too!

06:37.740 --> 06:39.680
Yeah, I seriously doubt that.

06:39.680 --> 06:43.820
So this cherry tree sucks the
lifeblood out of beastmen, bear-o...

06:43.820 --> 06:45.580
That's impossible, bear-o.

06:45.580 --> 06:47.120
It's obviously just a supersti...

06:47.120 --> 06:48.350
Bear-o!

06:50.660 --> 06:53.090
So you're actually scared, Toppy?

06:53.090 --> 06:54.930
Now why would I be scared, bear-o?!

06:54.930 --> 06:57.830
Just quit it with your stupid tricks, bear-o!

06:59.930 --> 07:02.000
I'm guessing this is bad?

07:02.000 --> 07:05.270
J-Just stay back, bear-o!

07:05.270 --> 07:07.670
What've you done?!

07:07.670 --> 07:10.880
Here's where you fess up and
tell him straight up you did it, bear-o.

07:10.880 --> 07:12.540
I think you're right.

07:12.540 --> 07:14.180
I'm sorry!

07:14.180 --> 07:16.540
I broke this branch off!

07:20.020 --> 07:22.210
What's wrong with him?

07:28.330 --> 07:31.690
Uh... I broke this off.

07:33.630 --> 07:36.230
That's enough of telling
them straight up, bear-o.

07:36.230 --> 07:38.800
Something's not right here, bear-o.

07:38.800 --> 07:41.910
I say we just hurry up and get our
food supplies and head on back, bear-o.

07:41.910 --> 07:43.130
Yeah?

07:57.920 --> 07:59.650
A human?!

08:04.260 --> 08:06.860
Who are... you?

08:08.370 --> 08:11.240
I apologize if I frightened you.

08:11.240 --> 08:15.070
But I made a promise to
meet up with someone here.

08:21.910 --> 08:24.080
What the heck is going on here, bear-o?!

08:24.080 --> 08:25.350
I'm guessing...

08:25.350 --> 08:29.690
maybe everyone actually believes the story
that cherry trees suck out their lifeblood.

08:29.690 --> 08:33.050
But that place looks like
they might sell us something.

08:35.090 --> 08:38.030
Excuse me, we'd like to buy some food...

08:38.030 --> 08:40.030
Stay away!

08:40.030 --> 08:43.030
Right this way!

08:43.030 --> 08:46.240
I've got a complete selection of
rare food items from all around the world.

08:46.240 --> 08:47.610
Hey, it's you!

08:47.610 --> 08:49.540
Agan the smuggler, bear-o!

08:49.540 --> 08:51.310
Oh, it's you guys.

08:51.310 --> 08:53.080
I guess we meet again.

08:53.080 --> 08:56.650
From the fact that you're here, I'm guessing you
managed to safely escape from the pleasure sh...

08:56.650 --> 08:57.620
What the...?!

08:57.620 --> 09:01.420
Is that from that cherry tree,
the last one left standing in town?!

09:01.420 --> 09:03.150
Yeah, sure is...

09:03.890 --> 09:05.990
You know something about it, bear-o?

09:05.990 --> 09:08.630
What's the deal with this cherry branch?

09:08.630 --> 09:11.500
Everyone takes off
running as soon as they see it.

09:11.500 --> 09:13.970
So you guys broke that branch off?

09:13.970 --> 09:16.830
Yeah, while we were
looking at the cherry blossoms.

09:16.830 --> 09:18.940
Well I mean, it was kind of an accident.

09:18.940 --> 09:21.810
That tree's called the Cursed Cherry Tree.

09:21.810 --> 09:24.940
All the beastmen around
here are scared to death of it.

09:24.940 --> 09:26.510
Th-The cursed Cherry Tree?!

09:26.510 --> 09:27.780
Yeah.

09:27.780 --> 09:29.750
Apparently anyone who tries to cut it down,

09:29.750 --> 09:32.180
or break off a branch,
or harm the tree in any way...

09:32.180 --> 09:36.950
will be cursed with one
terrifying misfortune after another.

09:36.950 --> 09:40.020
Apparently a large number of
beastmen have already died because of it.

09:40.020 --> 09:43.090
And that's why that cherry tree's
the only one left standing in town.

09:43.090 --> 09:44.830
No one'll dare cut it down or lay a hand on it.

09:44.830 --> 09:47.430
B-But no one told us!

09:47.430 --> 09:49.830
There's no reason to take it seriously, bear-o.

09:49.830 --> 09:53.940
It's just one of those town legends, r-right?

09:53.940 --> 09:58.040
Well I don't believe it myself, but...

09:58.040 --> 09:59.710
If it's food you want,
go bring me that one over there.

09:59.710 --> 10:01.710
Thank you!

10:01.710 --> 10:05.680
But you know what they say...
there's no smoke without fire.

10:05.680 --> 10:07.390
So I'd at least be careful if I were you.

10:07.390 --> 10:08.820
That's a good point.

10:08.820 --> 10:11.290
As long as we're careful we should be just fi...!

10:15.530 --> 10:18.650
Gwelp me... Tompmy!

10:20.130 --> 10:22.300
We're in big trouble, Morte!

10:22.300 --> 10:24.970
They say this cherry tree's cursed!

10:24.970 --> 10:26.670
What should we do?

10:26.670 --> 10:28.340
Huh?

10:28.340 --> 10:31.080
Like I... just... told you!

10:31.080 --> 10:33.010
It's a cursed tree so if we break off a branch

10:33.010 --> 10:35.680
or hurt it in any way we'll be
cursed with terrible misfortunes and!

10:35.680 --> 10:38.580
Um... well...

10:42.420 --> 10:45.220
We're getting sucked
deeper and deeper in, bear-o!

10:45.220 --> 10:47.660
You don't have to get so
worked up about it... you'll be fine.

10:47.660 --> 10:48.590
Huh?

10:48.590 --> 10:50.230
Who's this guy?

10:50.230 --> 10:51.660
It's a pleasure to meet you.

10:51.660 --> 10:53.230
My name is Jade.

10:53.230 --> 10:55.400
I live in the forest just
on the other side of the hill.

10:55.400 --> 10:58.200
I was the one who spread
the story of the curse around town.

10:58.200 --> 11:00.440
It's just a made-up story.

11:00.440 --> 11:02.510
So you can rest easy.

11:02.510 --> 11:05.580
Trust me, no harm will befall you.

11:05.580 --> 11:10.280
Why would you go around spreading
a made-up story like that, bear-o?

11:10.280 --> 11:12.380
In order to protect this cherry tree...

11:12.380 --> 11:15.580
from the axes of the beastmen.

11:17.190 --> 11:20.420
Are you a human who smuggles goods?

11:20.420 --> 11:22.590
Who are you people?

11:22.590 --> 11:25.730
We're from the World Salvation Committee.

11:25.730 --> 11:29.470
Have you run across any members
of the World Destruction Committee?

11:29.470 --> 11:32.700
You want information, you gotta pay up.

11:32.700 --> 11:35.040
Or you could just buy something
from me, if that's what you prefer.

11:35.040 --> 11:39.980
Do you have any idea who you're speaking to?!

11:39.980 --> 11:44.750
In that case, how about we take one
of those dried sand shark fins over there?

11:44.750 --> 11:46.740
And you can keep the change.

11:49.820 --> 11:52.720
Now that you mention it,
I did run into those guys here.

11:52.720 --> 11:56.130
But you'll think twice about getting
close to them if you know what's best for you.

11:56.130 --> 11:59.560
They stupidly broke a branch
off of the Cursed Cherry Tree.

11:59.560 --> 12:01.270
Cursed Cherry Tree?

12:01.270 --> 12:02.670
That's right.

12:02.670 --> 12:07.910
And if you two aren't careful, you
might wind up catching some of their bad luck!

12:07.910 --> 12:09.840
There's no need to worry about us.

12:09.840 --> 12:13.180
Curses and bad luck... and
other unscientific causes like that...

12:13.180 --> 12:15.110
simply don't exist.

12:18.350 --> 12:23.750
The truth is, I once promised to
meet someone under this very cherry tree.

12:23.750 --> 12:25.590
A woman, bear-o?

12:25.590 --> 12:28.530
Yes, she was my girlfriend.

12:28.530 --> 12:32.860
We used to live quietly
in a little village in Bonak.

12:32.860 --> 12:37.840
But one day, the beastmen came
and suddenly set fire to the village.

12:37.840 --> 12:41.810
All the men of the village
fought bravely to save it...

12:41.810 --> 12:44.710
but we had no hope of defeating the beastmen.

12:44.710 --> 12:46.540
So just before the final charge...

12:46.540 --> 12:49.150
the two of us made a promise.

12:49.150 --> 12:51.520
If both of us made it safely away...

12:51.520 --> 12:52.850
we'd find our way to the spring continent...

12:52.850 --> 12:55.120
to a hill just outside a town near the water...

12:55.120 --> 12:57.820
and meet under a cherry tree.

12:59.890 --> 13:01.690
And so?

13:01.690 --> 13:05.360
Were you able to finally
reunite with your girlfriend?

13:05.360 --> 13:06.700
No...

13:06.700 --> 13:11.190
and that's why I can't allow
this cherry tree to disappear.

13:12.800 --> 13:16.070
But... today was another day, and...

13:16.070 --> 13:18.800
it seems she hasn't quite made it yet.

13:35.530 --> 13:37.830
Well anyway, it's a good thing, bear-o.

13:37.830 --> 13:41.860
I'm glad things like bad luck and
curses just don't exist in the world, bear-o.

13:43.400 --> 13:45.740
But it's not a good thing at all, Toppy!

13:45.740 --> 13:47.440
Why's that, bear-o?

13:47.440 --> 13:53.210
Because by now everyone in the town knows
that I broke a branch off of this cherry tree.

13:53.210 --> 13:55.180
And if nothing bad happens because of it...

13:55.180 --> 13:59.120
they're gonna figure out that the rumor
Jade worked so hard to spread was just a lie!

13:59.120 --> 14:03.220
Well, I think it's still too soon to
say that nothing bad will happen...

14:03.220 --> 14:09.630
You never know... some kind of unbelievably
terrible misfortune could still befall us!

14:09.630 --> 14:11.630
What are you saying, bear-o?

14:11.630 --> 14:15.600
Morte, are you the kind of
person who believes in that stuff?

14:15.600 --> 14:17.640
I guess I am...

14:17.640 --> 14:21.570
At any rate, it's a fact that the bad luck
and curse in this case was a lie, bear-o.

14:21.570 --> 14:23.940
And there's nothing we can
do about that now, bear-o!

14:26.210 --> 14:27.780
But the way things are now...

14:27.780 --> 14:31.450
this cherry tree could wind up getting cut down!

14:31.450 --> 14:33.120
We've just...

14:33.120 --> 14:36.110
We've just gotta do something...

14:38.460 --> 14:42.230
"Aah! Bird poop just landed on me!"

14:42.230 --> 14:48.400
"Eek! Ow! Now a potted
plant just fell on my head!"

14:48.400 --> 14:50.000
What the heck is this, bear-o?

14:50.000 --> 14:52.240
What do you mean "what"? It's a script.

14:52.240 --> 14:54.610
You spent the whole night thinking
about what you can do to fix things...

14:54.610 --> 14:56.240
and this is what you came up with?!

14:56.240 --> 14:59.440
That's right! If there's
no real curse or bad luck...

14:59.440 --> 15:01.480
we can just make some up!

15:01.480 --> 15:04.010
First, we've gotta do it where
there's a lot of people around...

15:04.010 --> 15:05.280
And oh yeah!

15:05.280 --> 15:07.790
It'll work better if the
Frog Master sees it too...

15:07.790 --> 15:09.590
so I think we should do it along the big avenue

15:09.590 --> 15:11.920
that passes right in front
of the town lord's mansion.

15:12.590 --> 15:15.930
So we go there and then bird
poop lands on your head, Toppy.

15:15.930 --> 15:17.830
Oh, and I'll be the one dropping it, okay?

15:17.830 --> 15:21.670
At that point you scream as loud as
you can and start making a scene.

15:21.670 --> 15:25.870
The Frog Master hears the ruckus and rushes
outside the mansion to see what's going on.

15:25.870 --> 15:28.640
That's when the potted
plant comes crashing down.

15:28.640 --> 15:30.510
I'll be the one dropping that, too.

15:30.510 --> 15:31.980
Now wait just a minute, bear-o!

15:31.980 --> 15:34.980
How come I'm the only one who
has to play the victim, bear-o?!

15:34.980 --> 15:36.350
There's no other way we can do it.

15:36.350 --> 15:39.480
Morte won't even help
out with this kind of thing.

15:39.480 --> 15:40.450
But don't worry!

15:40.450 --> 15:43.320
At the very end I'll pretend
to die right along with you.

15:44.890 --> 15:48.330
So Toppy, you start screaming
again and make a run for the canal.

15:48.330 --> 15:49.890
At that point you join up with me...

15:49.890 --> 15:52.130
and say, "Let's get out of this town quick!"

15:52.130 --> 15:53.060
You scream it.

15:53.060 --> 15:55.000
Then we hop onto a boat we'll have ready there.

15:55.000 --> 15:57.800
But the boat's already
got a hole in the bottom...

16:04.040 --> 16:08.250
I don't see why I have to go along
with this cheapjack theatrical farce, bear-o!

16:08.250 --> 16:10.050
Just calm down now, calm down.

16:10.050 --> 16:14.250
We're doing this so Jade will still
be able to reunite with his girlfriend!

16:14.250 --> 16:16.420
Don't tell me you're actually using real poop?!

16:16.420 --> 16:19.220
It's important to have
realism with this kind of thing.

16:19.220 --> 16:22.060
All right, birdy-bird... squeeze it out hard!

16:23.160 --> 16:25.560
What's taking so long, bear-o?

16:27.060 --> 16:29.000
Well, that's strange...

16:29.000 --> 16:31.440
I wonder if this bird already went...

16:31.440 --> 16:34.600
Those guys are from the
World Salvation Committee, bear-o!

16:37.740 --> 16:41.680
It worked, Toppy!
Now hurry up and let out a shriek!

16:41.680 --> 16:44.910
Looks like I found them!

16:50.290 --> 16:54.020
You stupid little brat!

17:01.270 --> 17:02.600
Get up, bear-o!

17:16.210 --> 17:18.280
What's going on here?

17:18.280 --> 17:20.270
Those are the ones from yesterday.

17:24.150 --> 17:26.950
Do things like that really happen?

17:44.510 --> 17:47.580
Toppy! Why are we just... running away?!

17:47.580 --> 17:49.110
If we defeat them now...

17:49.110 --> 17:49.850
Whoa!...

17:49.850 --> 17:52.520
that script you worked so
hard on will be ruined, bear-o...

17:52.520 --> 17:53.420
Bear-whoa!

17:53.420 --> 17:56.480
But it's already ruined!

17:57.920 --> 17:59.920
This part may be different
from the original script...

17:59.920 --> 18:03.360
but we can still make our escape
by pretending to drown to death, bear-o!

18:28.550 --> 18:30.540
You sure this is gonna work?!

18:31.220 --> 18:34.190
- She can't come after us on
the surface of the water, bear-o!
- Wait! I won't let you escape!

18:34.190 --> 18:36.460
- Now we just find an appropriate spot...
- You think I'll just take
your bird poop lying down?!

18:36.460 --> 18:38.700
Where we pretend to drown to death...

18:38.700 --> 18:41.190
and we're home free, bear-o!

18:45.240 --> 18:47.700
Where'd he get that, bear-o?!

18:49.470 --> 18:51.170
Get in, Lia!

18:58.180 --> 18:59.080
This is bad!

18:59.080 --> 18:59.720
Toppy!

18:59.720 --> 19:00.650
We need...

19:00.650 --> 19:01.920
more speed!

19:01.920 --> 19:02.850
We're screwed, bear-o!

19:02.850 --> 19:05.550
At this rate they'll catch up, bear-o!

19:16.730 --> 19:17.840
What's all the commotion?

19:17.840 --> 19:20.600
What's all the commotion?!

19:24.740 --> 19:26.840
Rib-bit!

19:41.560 --> 19:43.090
Waah! Help us!

19:43.090 --> 19:45.130
I knew it... it's our bad luck for
breaking off that cherry branch!

19:45.130 --> 19:46.630
Help us, bear-o!

19:46.630 --> 19:49.430
We'll drown to death
because of the curse, bear-o!

20:03.880 --> 20:05.720
It seems to have worked like a charm.

20:05.720 --> 20:08.720
Yeah, I'm sure everyone believed it.

20:08.720 --> 20:12.790
I think that cherry tree'll be safe from now on.

20:12.790 --> 20:14.290
Thank you.

20:14.290 --> 20:18.800
When that bridge collapsed,
was that just a coincidence, bear-o?

20:18.800 --> 20:20.660
Well, it wasn't a curse or bad luck...

20:20.660 --> 20:25.400
but perhaps it's safe to say
a greater force was at work.

20:27.000 --> 20:29.240
So are they dead?

20:29.240 --> 20:30.570
No...

20:30.570 --> 20:35.140
From the looks of it, I'd say they
got away from us... slicker than slick.

20:36.410 --> 20:42.350
But I wonder... how long has Jade
been waiting for his girlfriend to show?

20:42.350 --> 20:44.120
I think...

20:44.120 --> 20:46.090
it's been decades now.

20:46.090 --> 20:47.320
Decades?!

20:47.320 --> 20:49.330
What does that mean, bear-o?

20:49.330 --> 20:54.600
That war between the beastmen and
humans in Bonak that Jade told us about...

20:54.600 --> 20:57.500
I heard the same story
from my father before he died.

20:57.500 --> 21:02.000
And he said it happened decades ago.

21:03.010 --> 21:08.150
So while you two were in town,
I went to go check out his story.

21:08.150 --> 21:12.050
I found Jade's house on
the other side of the hill.

21:13.350 --> 21:18.290
But Jade himself had been dead for years.

21:18.290 --> 21:22.630
I'm sure he waited day
after day under this cherry tree...

21:22.630 --> 21:25.990
without ever being able
to see his girlfriend again.

21:27.130 --> 21:28.470
So that means...

21:28.470 --> 21:31.570
the Jade that we met was!

21:31.570 --> 21:33.870
Even after his death...

21:33.870 --> 21:35.510
Jade protected this cherry tree...

21:35.510 --> 21:39.030
and kept waiting for his beloved, bear-o.

21:45.750 --> 21:50.310
I wonder if Jade's spirit will ever
get to reunite with his girlfriend.

21:51.660 --> 21:54.990
I'm sure as long as that
cherry tree continues to bloom...

21:54.990 --> 21:58.020
one day they'll meet again, bear-o.

22:21.080 --> 22:24.590
Kirameku suna no umi

22:24.590 --> 22:27.720
Aoi chijou no hate

22:27.720 --> 22:33.800
Yuuyami ni ochita sora kara

22:33.800 --> 22:36.930
afuredasu kioku

22:36.930 --> 22:40.140
Gareki no you ni

22:40.140 --> 22:46.140
kasanete yuku darou

22:46.140 --> 22:49.380
Meguriau inochi

22:49.380 --> 22:52.450
Surechigau kimochi

22:52.450 --> 22:55.590
Tsumugiau kotoba

22:55.590 --> 22:58.720
Kizutsukeau mono

22:58.720 --> 23:10.830
Sore demo bokura ga aruiteku
michi wa asu e tsuzuiteru no

23:13.670 --> 23:17.510
Ima o against the world ikiru imi wa

23:17.510 --> 23:20.510
change the world hitotsu janai

23:20.510 --> 23:26.080
Namima no mukou haruka na tabi e

23:26.080 --> 23:29.650
Dakara around the world ikiru kodou

23:29.650 --> 23:33.190
To the end of the world kaze ni hibike

23:33.190 --> 23:39.160
Sono saki ni aru

23:39.160 --> 23:50.770
yakusoku no chi, tadoritsukeru made

23:52.340 --> 23:54.480
I get separated from Kyrie and Morte...

23:54.480 --> 23:58.350
and meet up with an old friend
in a town with a huge coliseum.

23:58.350 --> 24:02.690
It's a reunion between friends who once vowed to
each other that we would be heroes among heroes.

24:02.690 --> 24:07.820
But as it turns out, he and
I didn't share the same vision.

24:07.820 --> 24:10.860
Next time on World Destruction... Episode 5:

24:10.860 --> 24:12.900
"There Are Two Kinds of Men."

24:12.900 --> 24:15.370
How come he's not ending his
sentences with "bear-o" anymore?

24:15.370 --> 24:18.340
Maybe because it's his inner voice... I think...

24:18.340 --> 24:19.830
Bear-o!
